  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "suppression; subjugation; gaining control",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "suppression; subjugation; gaining control by force",
      "explanation": "Using force or authority to bring a situation, area, or group under control. Often used in military, security, and sports contexts."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "23059_seiatsu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{暴動|ぼうどう}を{制圧|せいあつ}する。",
      "english": "To suppress a riot.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "23059_seiatsu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{警察|けいさつ}が{現場|げんば}を{制圧|せいあつ}した。",
      "english": "The police gained control of the scene.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "23059_seiatsu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{相手|あいて}チームを{圧倒的|あっとうてき}な{攻撃力|こうげきりょく}で{制圧|せいあつ}した。",
      "english": "They dominated the opposing team with overwhelming offensive power.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound of {制|せい} (control/restrain) + {圧|あつ} (pressure). Implies the use of force or overwhelming power to bring something under control.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {制圧|せいあつ}する: to suppress, to subdue\n- {武力|ぶりょく}{制圧|せいあつ}: armed suppression\n- {制圧|せいあつ}{射撃|しゃげき}: suppressive fire\n- {完全|かんぜん}{制圧|せいあつ}: complete subjugation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {鎮圧|ちんあつ}: suppression, quelling — focuses on calming a disturbance\n- {制御|せいぎょ}: control — managing or regulating something (less forceful)\n- {征服|せいふく}: conquest — complete subjugation of a people or territory\n- {弾圧|だんあつ}: oppression — suppressing people or movements through force",
